<span class="line"><span>Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) are a type of artificial neural network that are commonly used in image recognition and classification tasks. They are inspired by the structure of the human brain and are composed of multiple layers of neurons connected in a specific pattern. The neurons in the first layer of a CNN are connected to the input image, and the neurons in the last layer are connected to the output. The neurons in between the input and output layers are called feature maps and are responsible for extracting features from the input image. CNNs use convolutional layers to detect patterns in the input image and pooling layers to reduce the size of the feature maps. This allows the CNN to learn the most important features in the image and use them to make predictions.</span></span>
